    {
      "id": "CA9KQzJGK7uRMLCymAJcA",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1959.480973697846,
      "y": 734.5759216649267,
      "width": 910.0891723632812,
      "height": 1100,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "EdphUBZ1rLxqf_xYsNDXa",
        "6KEdnU9c9txDYqDQKvRdq",
        "c3ePegDpquu-9JTbTURKf",
        "41YBo0RqHs4crI1GHUmO_"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aU",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 326894214,
      "version": 4371,
      "versionNonce": 80890202,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790248994049,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Qwen-Audio is designed to give large language models the ability to understand sound, \nnot just text. The key idea is to take a powerful language model (Qwen-7B) and connect \nit to an audio perception system so that the model can listen to speech, music,\nenvironmental sounds, and many other kinds of audio, and then reason or answer questions\nabout them.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nQwen-Audio contains an audio encoder and a large language model.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nAudio Encoder\nQwen-Audio employs a single audio encoder initialized from Whisper-large-v2 encoder (640M,\n32 layers)\n\nAudio is converted into a numerical representation, broken into small time chunks, and then\ncompressed into meaningful features by the encoder. Sound --> dense enbedding\n\nLanguage Decoder\nThe model is initialized using pre-trained weights derived from Qwen-7B",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Qwen-Audio is designed to give large language models the ability to understand sound, \nnot just text. The key idea is to take a powerful language model (Qwen-7B) and connect \nit to an audio perception system so that the model can listen to speech, music, environmental sounds, and many other kinds of audio, and then reason or answer questions about them.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nQwen-Audio contains an audio encoder and a large language model.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nAudio Encoder\nQwen-Audio employs a single audio encoder initialized from Whisper-large-v2 encoder (640M, 32 layers)\n\nAudio is converted into a numerical representation, broken into small time chunks, and then compressed into meaningful features by the encoder. Sound --> dense enbedding\n\nLanguage Decoder\nThe model is initialized using pre-trained weights derived from Qwen-7B",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
